# Sherlock Holmes, The Index mode only. bin/compose-agents.sh reads this file;
# the format is in that script's header.
name: holmes-index
source: holmes
description: Sherlock Holmes in The Index mode only — the item-ID token in, one App-signed verdict on the item's PR out. Dispatch workbench-dev-team:holmes, which routes the token here.

requires: Agent, Bash, Read, Grep, Glob

section: # Sherlock Holmes — Code Review Agent
section: ## How you write
section: ## When a gate or guard refuses you
section: ## Scratch folders — make them in a scratch root, delete them yourself
skip: ## Mode detection
section: ## The Index-mode input contract
skip: ## The brief contract — refuse an incomplete brief, ask about a vague one
text: ## Input — a dispatch token, never a brief
text:
text: This prompt is The Index mode of `workbench-dev-team:holmes`. It takes only
text: the machine-built token `Item ID: <n>`, never a six-slot brief. If your
text: prompt carries no such token, it reached the wrong type: change nothing, and
text: report that `workbench-dev-team:holmes` takes the brief.
section: ## Working-context budget — roughly 250k tokens, self-checked
section: ## Tools
section: ## Tools — The Index mode
skip: ## Local mode
section: ## The Index-mode workflow
section: ### 0. Read the config (fan-out knobs)
section: ### 1. Fetch the item
section: ### 2. Find the PR
section: ### 2.5. Decision request? (answer mode — before reviewing code)
section: ### 3. Compute the strike count — informs §5, never skips the review
section: ### 4. Review the PR
section: #### Phase A — set up the evidence
section: ##### 4a. Read the issue and AC
section: ##### 4a.5. Search `feedback/` before you judge — required, in both modes
section: ##### 4b. Check out the PR — the shared evidence room
section: ##### 4c. Confirm the tests passed — trust CI, don't re-run
section: #### Phases B, C, and D — fan-out, adversarial verification, memory context
section: #### 4d. Check conformance against the acceptance criteria — the contract
section: #### 4e. Defects and observations beyond the AC — route by the coherent unit of work, then coupling and locality
section: ### 5. Submit your verdict — three outcomes, and only three
section: #### 🕰️ Before you write anything — re-read the item
section: #### ✅ APPROVE — every AC item met, no hard defect anywhere, and the PR's own code **plus everything belonging to the coherent unit** carry no actionable finding
section: #### 🔄 REQUEST CHANGES — an AC item is unmet (impl wrong/incomplete), a hard defect surfaced, or the PR's own code **or anything belonging to the coherent unit** carries an actionable finding
section: #### 🛑 ESCALATE — the **AC itself** looks wrong/imprecise/impossible/contradicted, **or** the impl diverges from an AC item in a way you can't confidently call a strict, nothing-dropped improvement
section: ### 5.5. Record review learnings — on every verdict
section: ### 6. Report
section: ## Rules
